{"result": {"id": "chatcmpl-408492a656e34d0ab4187a771fd92a36", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "{\n    \"title\": \"SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2025\",\n    \"summary\": \"This report provides an overview of SAP's cloud services, highlighting key components, their environments, and recent updates. The information is relevant to SAP's cloud operations as of 2025.\",\n    \"rating\": 8.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The high importance rating reflects the critical roles that SAP's cloud services play in supporting the company's digital transformation and customer needs, with a focus on innovation, security, and compliance.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Cloud Logging and Monitoring\",\n            \"explanation\": \"SAP Cloud Logging and Monitoring services provide real-time insights into cloud operations, enabling proactive issue resolution and improved customer experience. Recent updates include enhanced stacktrace display and improved logging capabilities. [Data: Sources (729, 730), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 04), (2025, 09, 04))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Cloud Transport Management\",\n            \"explanation\": \"SAP Cloud Transport Management enables secure and efficient transportation of data between cloud environments. Recent updates include integration with SAP Asset Performance Management, modifiable transport requests, and a new ImportSelectedOperator role. [Data: Sources (202, 203, 204), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 26), (2025, 08, 26))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"SAP Build Process Automation\",\n            \"explanation\": \"SAP Build Process Automation enables customers to automate business processes and workflows. Recent updates include behavior changes to task instances REST APIs, the ability to download model for guided process definitions, and advanced functions for decisions. [Data: Sources (205, 206, 207), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 26), (2025, 08, 26))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Cloud Identity Services\",\n            \"explanation\": \"SAP Cloud Identity Services provide secure identity and access management for cloud applications. Recent updates include the deprecation of the SAP Ariba Category Management connector and improved REST APIs for application logging. [Data: Sources (208, 209), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 12), (2025, 08, 25))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Continuous Integration and Delivery\",\n            \"explanation\": \"SAP Continuous Integration and Delivery services enable customers to automate testing, deployment, and delivery of cloud applications. Recent updates include increased quotas, deprecation of the Container-Based Applications pipeline, and improved REST APIs for application logging. [Data: Sources (1533, 1534, 1535), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 28), (2025, 01, 28))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"SAP Document AI\",\n            \"explanation\": \"SAP Document AI provides AI-powered document processing and analysis capabilities. Recent updates include support for new file types, support for the Identity Authentication Service, and improved REST APIs for application logging. [Data: Sources (1536, 1537), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 28), (2025, 01, 28))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Joule\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Joule is a conversational AI platform that enables customers to automate business processes and workflows. Recent updates include the introduction of a new conversational experience and improved REST APIs for application logging. [Data: Sources (1539), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 17), (2025, 01, 27))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"SAP Task Center\",\n            \"explanation\": \"SAP Task Center provides a centralized platform for task management and automation. Recent updates include improved back navigation, new transition guide, and improved REST APIs for application logging. [Data: Sources (1532, 207), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 29), (2025, 08, 26))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Variant Configuration\",\n            \"explanation\": \"SAP Variant Configuration provides a platform for product configuration and pricing. Recent updates include improved API for configurations and improved REST APIs for application logging. [Data: Sources (248), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 27), (2025, 08, 27))]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"date_range\": [\"2025-01-01\", \"2025-09-04\"]\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [], "reasoning_content": null}, "stop_reason": null, "token_ids": null}], "created": 1758949397, "model": "unsloth/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 967, "prompt_tokens": 5900, "total_tokens": 6867, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": null}, "prompt_logprobs": null, "prompt_token_ids": null, "kv_transfer_params": null}, "input": {"messages": [{"content": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery.\nInformation discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims.\nThe report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact.\nThe content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their core attributes or capabilities, their connections, and noteworthy claims.\nRetain as much time specific information as possible so your end user can build a timeline of events.\n\n# Report Structure\nThe report should include the following sections:\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title. Avoid including phrases like 'eligibility assessment' or 'eligibility assessment report' in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant program-specific or eligibility-related insights.\n- IMPORTANCE RATING: A float score between 0-10 that represents the importance of entities within the community..\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the importance rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n- DATE RANGE: A range of dates (YYYY-MM-DD) with the format [START, END] which corresponds to the date range of text units and intermediate reports used to build the report.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format. Don't use any unnecessary escape sequences. The output should be a single JSON object that can be parsed by json.loads.\n    {\n        \"title\": \"<report_title>\",\n        \"summary\": \"<executive_summary>\",\n        \"rating\": <importance_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": \"<rating_explanation>\",\n        \"findings\": [{\"summary\":\"<insight_1_summary>\", \"explanation\": \"<insight_1_explanation\"}, {\"summary\":\"<insight_2_summary>\", \"explanation\": \"<insight_2_explanation\"}],\n\t\t\"date_range\": [\"<date range start>\", \"<date range end>\"],\n\n    }\n\n# Grounding Rules\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids), <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X resolved a major issue with project Y [Data: Sources (1, 5),  Date_Range ((2001, 05, 12), (2001, 05, 14))]. He also made major updates to the database of app Y [Data: Reports (2, 4), Sources (7, 23, 2, 34, 46, +more), Date_Range ((2001, 05, 15), (2001, 05, 18))\"\"\n\nwhere 1, 2, 4, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, and 46 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nLimit the total report length to 2000 words.\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nSOURCES\nid, text\n1, Text: From: compliance.office@enron.com To: management.team@enron.com Cc: legal.team@enron.com, risk@enron.com Date: Wed, 12 Jul 2000 08:30:00 -0600 (CST) Subject: Quick Update on Compliance & Risk Efforts\n2, Quick update on what's been cooking in Compliance and Risk Management. Risk Management is stepping up — They've been tightening up on our financial risk assessments and mitigation strategies since early this year.\n3, Their efforts are key to keeping us on solid ground financially and in compliance with the latest market regulations as of mid-2000. It's crucial for our strategic planning and helps us stay ahead.\n5, Legal's keeping us in check — The Legal Compliance team is on top of ensuring all our operations are up to scratch with legal standards. They're especially focused on improving our corporate governance and contract management as of the second quarter of 2000. This is critical for keeping our operations smooth and legally sound.\n9, Working together — Risk Management and Legal Compliance have been syncing up better than ever since the start of Q2 2000. They're making sure our strategies are not just effective but also fully compliant. This coordination is essential for our integrated governance approach.\n10, Your thoughts? — How do these updates impact your area? Got ideas on how we can do better? Give your department heads a shout.\n11, Thanks for staying engaged. Let's keep pushing for better and smarter ways to work. Cheers, Jane Doe\n\nOutput:\n\n{\n    \"title\": \"Enron Compliance and Risk Management Overview as of July 2000\",\n    \"summary\": \"This report delves into Enron's key departments focusing on compliance and risk management, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2000.\",\n    \"rating\": 9.2,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The high importance rating reflects the critical roles that the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments play in ensuring Enron's adherence to financial and legal regulations, crucial for maintaining the company's integrity and operational stability.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Risk Management Operational Scope\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Risk Management Department at Enron plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2000, helps safeguard Enron against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes.\n\n[Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2000, 01, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Legal Compliance and Governance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Legal Compliance Department ensures that all Enron's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2000, is crucial in maintaining Enron's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices.\n\n[Data: Source (5), Date_Range ((2000, 04, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Collaboration between the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments, established in Q2 2000, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at Enron. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements.\n\n[Data: Sources (9), Date_Range ((2000, 04, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"date_range\": [\"2000-01-01\", \"2000-07-12\"]\n}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----SOURCES-----\nid,text,entity_degree\n729,\"--- Record 151 ---\nComponent: Cloud Logging\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Array based stacktraces in the field stacktrace will now be displayed correctly\nDescription: Array based stacktraces in the field stacktrace will now be displayed correctly\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-04\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 152 ---\nComponent: Cloud Logging\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Other\nTitle: Fixed traceID link in the OpenTelemetry index patterns for instances using OpenSearch 2.x (\"\"explore\"\" phase)\nDescription: The traceID link in the Open Telemetry index patterns for instances using OpenSearch in the Explore phase have been fixed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-04\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 153 ---\nComponent: Cloud Logging\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Other\nTitle: OpenSearch and OpenSearch Dashboards update to version 2.19.3 for instances in \"\"explore\"\" phase\nDescription: The SAP Cloud Logging service has now updated the OpenSearch and OpenSearch Dashboards to version 2.19.3 for instances in explore phase.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-04\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 154 ---\nComponent: Cloud Management Tools,SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Enhanced Cost Transparency in SAP BTP Cockpit with Direct Access to SAP Price List\nDescription: You can now access the general SAP Price List directly from the Global Account Info card in the header of the Costs and Usage page in SAP BTP Cockpit.   You can also easily open the SAP Price List for a specific service from the Billing tab using the Actions context menu or the service's details in both the View by Service and View by Account views.  See Monitoring Usage and Consumption Costs in Your Global Account.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-04\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 155 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Modifiable transport requests\nDescription: UI enhancements to the modifiable transport requests function.   New blog post announcing modifiable transport requests.  See:   Processing Modifiable Transport Requests  Blog post: Modifiable Transport Requests now also for your SAP cloud changes    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-04\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: 2508b\n\n--- Record 156 ---\nComponent: Custom Domain Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SaaS Applications with SAP Identity Service-Based User Authentication\nDescription: In Custom Domain Manager, SaaS routes can now be created for SaaS applications with SAP Identity Service-based user authentication. For more information, see SaaS Applications with SAP Identity Service-Based User Authentication.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-04\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 157 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Keda module: Update to version 1.8.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:    The runtime images installed by keda-manager can now be localized, enabling deployment in regulated environments with restricted or private registries.  The version of the managed Keda installation is now available for inspection in the Keda CR status.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-21\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 158 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Serverless module: Update to version 1.8.0\nDescription: Buildless Mode (beta): This version of the Serverless module introduces an optional buildless mode (beta), significantly reducing Function startup times by eliminating the image build and push step.  In buildless mode, Function code and dependencies are injected directly into Kyma-provided runtime images at Pod startup.  You can toggle on or off buildless mode by changing the Serverless configuration and choosing the best approach for your use case. For more details, see Serverless Buildless Mode.  Starting with the 1.9.0 release, buildless mode will be switched on by default, with the option to disable it manually. From the 2.0.0 version, buildless mode will be the only available option.  Localizable Serverless Images:Serverless runtime images can now be localized, enabling deployment in environments with restricted or private registries.  This enhancement improves flexibility and compliance for enterprise and regulated workloads.  Dedicated Network Policies:With version 1.8.0, users can enable dedicated Serverless network policies. This ensures Serverless remains functional on clusters with restrictive, deny-all network policies, improving security and compatibility for enterprise environments.  Deprecations/Breaking changes:The following fields, that were\",1376\n730,\"izable Serverless Images:Serverless runtime images can now be localized, enabling deployment in environments with restricted or private registries.  This enhancement improves flexibility and compliance for enterprise and regulated workloads.  Dedicated Network Policies:With version 1.8.0, users can enable dedicated Serverless network policies. This ensures Serverless remains functional on clusters with restrictive, deny-all network policies, improving security and compatibility for enterprise environments.  Deprecations/Breaking changes:The following fields, that were deprecated in the Serverless 1.6.0 release are no longer functional in buildless mode:    Function CRD  spec.scaleConfig – For existing Functions with scaleConfig defined, the HorizontalPodAutoscaler objects are not deleted upon switching to buildless mode, but are no longer managed by the Serverless module. To learn how to scale Functions, see Use External Scalers.  spec.resourceConfiguration.build    Serverless CRD  spec.dockerRegistry  spec.targetCPUUtilizationPercentage  spec.functionBuildExecutorArgs  spec.functionBuildMaxSimultaneousJobs  spec.defaultBuildJobPreset    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-02\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 159 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kubernetes,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: New UI Languages\nDescription: You can now use the SAP BTP cockpit in four additional languages:      French (Français)  German (Deutsch)  Portuguese (Português)  Spanish (Español)      To change your language: Navigate to your profile icon in the header, then go to Settings  Language.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-04\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 160 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 51.2.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 51.0.0 to 51.2.0.    https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v51.2.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v51.1.0  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-04\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: 2508b\n\n\",593\n107,\"--- Record 1531 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Keda module: Update to version 1.6.0\nDescription: In this release, we have updated KEDA to version 2.16.1.  In addition, we have added the status widget with conditions to the details view in Kyma dashboard for Keda CR and ScaledObject CR.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-16\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1532 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Task Center Improvements\nDescription:   Improved the back navigation when returning from the Substitution Management screen in the SAP Task Center Web app.  Internal optimizations and refactoring to ensure performance, security, and future improvements.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1533 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deprecation of MTA Build Tool Version Java 8 Node 18\nDescription: The MTA build tool version Java 8 Node 18 is deprecated and has been removed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deleted\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-28\nValid as Of: 2025-01-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1534 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deprecation of the Container-Based Applications Pipeline\nDescription:  The Container-Based Applications pipeline has been deprecated and is no longer available for use. While your existing jobs can still be viewed, you will not be able to run or edit them anymore.  We recommend using the Kyma Runtime pipeline instead.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deleted\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-28\nValid as Of: 2025-01-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1535 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Increased Quotas\nDescription: For the default and build-code service plans, the limit of job configurations and the maximum number of connected repositories have been increased from 500 to 1000.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-28\nValid as Of: 2025-01-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1536 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support for New File Types (Premium Edition)\nDescription: SAP Document AI now supports businessCard, invoice, paymentAdvice, purchaseOrder, and custom documents in the following file types:  DOC  DOCM  DOCX  DOT  DOTM  DOTX  EML  EMLX  MSG  ODT  OFT  OLM  PAGES  RTF  TXT    See Supported File Types (Embedded Edition and Premium Edition).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-28\nValid as Of: 2025-01-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1537 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support for the Identity Authentication Service\nDescription: You can now subscribe to the SAP Document AI basic UI using the Identity Authentication service to handle authentication and authorization tasks in SAP BTP.  See Subscribing to the SAP Document AI Basic UI With the Identity Authentication Service.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-28\nValid as Of: 2025-01-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1538 ---\nComponent: UI Theme Designer\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Theming Base Content for CF and Neo.\nDescription: The base theming content is updated to version 11.25.0. Review the changes at https://github.com/SAP/theming-base-content/releases.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-01-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1539 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: All SAP SuccessFactors Use Cases Upgraded to New Conversational Experience in Joule\nDescription: Based on the new conversational experience, SAP SuccessFactors has introduced a new transactional use case and upgraded all remaining cases. For more information, refer to All Use Cases Upgraded to New Conversational Experience in Joule.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Human Resources\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-17\nValid as Of: 2025-01-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1540 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Advanced Functions for Decisions\nDescription: You can now use two new functions, SUBSTRING and STRINGREPLACE in your decisions. See Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-27\nValid as Of: 2025-01-27\",274\n248,\"--- Record 201 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configurations API - Avoid Retry When Using Inactive Knowledge Bases\nDescription: An internal retry logic used to be applied to requests which failed because the corresponding knowledge base was inactive, which led to long response times. This issue has been corrected.  A knowledge base can become inactive if a customer triggers a reload from the administration UI by specifying a valid-from date later than the valid-from date of the used knowledge base.  See Administration Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-27\nValid as Of: 2025-08-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 202 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration of SAP Asset Performance Management with SAP Cloud Transport Management\nDescription: You can now use SAP Cloud Transport Management to transport SAP Asset Performance management content.  See:   Supported Content Types  Integrating SAP Cloud Transport Management with Other SAP Cloud Solutions  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-26\nValid as Of: 2025-08-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 203 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Modifiable transport requests\nDescription: You can create transport requests that are initially empty. You can use them to add multiple files and test the deployment of the files. After successful testing, you can release the transport requests. As a result, they become available for import.  See:   Processing Modifiable Transport Requests  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-26\nValid as Of: 2025-08-26\nVersion: 2508a\n\n--- Record 204 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New ImportSelectedOperator role\nDescription: Use this role if you want to enable users to import selected transport requests in an import queue, but not all requests.  See:   Security  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-26\nValid as Of: 2025-08-26\nVersion: 2508a\n\n--- Record 205 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Behavior Changes of Task Instances REST APIs\nDescription: According to the latest update, APIs for patching and retrieving task contexts are corrected. As a result, task context is now independent of workflow contexts right after input evaluation. The system now ensures this independence, whereas previously it relied solely on modelling best practices.The system processes follow-up actions after completing a task asynchronously. In rare cases, errors from Forms and Approval Forms may now appear on the Logs section of the Instance Details view instead of coming through the API responses. Only users with the Administrator role can see the logs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-26\nValid as Of: 2025-08-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 206 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Download Model for Guided Process Definitions\nDescription: You can now download the latest deployed version of the Guided Process definition. See Processes and Workflows.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-26\nValid as Of: 2025-08-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 207 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Transition